# Centralized DHCP Configuration

Architecture
One DHCP server (Server1-DHCPDNS, 10.10.180.10) in VLAN 180 serves all VLANs. Each VLAN uses DHCP relay (ip helper-address) on its SVI on both core switches to forward requests to the server. This keeps the network simple and centralized, instead of needing a separate DHCP server for each VLAN.

Configure DHCP Relay on Both Core Switches
Adds ip helper-address 10.10.180.10 to every VLAN's SVI, so DHCP broadcasts from any department get forwarded to the real server regardless of which core switch is currently active for that VLAN.

